---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj16.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Significant Influence — the Threshold for Equity Method Application" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Mechanics — Adjusting the Investment for the Investor's Share of Profit/Loss" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Elimination of Unrealised Profits on Transactions With Affiliates" },
        { id: "s6", label: "A DISTINCTIVE FEATURE — Equity Method Applies Only in Consolidated Statements" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — Recognising the Investor's Share of Affiliate Profit" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Eliminating an Unrealised Intercompany Profit" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">
<div class="section-header" id="s1">
  <span class="num">1</span>
  <h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card ci span2">
    <div class="ctitle ci">Sharing in an affiliate's economic performance, without full consolidation</div>
    <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 16 governs the EQUITY METHOD (持分法) — a measurement approach applied to investments in ENTITIES over which the investor has SIGNIFICANT INFLUENCE (typically affiliates and certain joint ventures) but NOT control. Rather than consolidating the investee LINE-BY-LINE (as with a subsidiary), the investor recognises its PROPORTIONATE SHARE of the investee's profit or loss (and OTHER equity changes) as an ADJUSTMENT to the CARRYING AMOUNT of a SINGLE investment line.</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s2">
  <span class="num">2</span>
  <h2>Scope</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cw span2">
    <div class="ctitle cw">Investments in affiliates and certain joint ventures within consolidated statements</div>
    <div class="principle">This Statement applies to investments in AFFILIATES (関連会社) — and certain JOINT VENTURE arrangements — within an entity's CONSOLIDATED financial statements, where the investor holds SIGNIFICANT INFLUENCE but not control.</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s3">
  <span class="num">3</span>
  <h2>Significant Influence — the Threshold for Equity Method Application</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cd span2">
    <div class="ctitle cd">Generally 20%–50% voting rights, or other qualitative indicators</div>
    <div class="text-supporting">SIGNIFICANT INFLUENCE is generally PRESUMED where the investor holds BETWEEN 20% and 50% of the investee's VOTING rights — though the assessment also considers QUALITATIVE indicators such as BOARD representation, PARTICIPATION in policy-making, MATERIAL transactions between the parties, INTERCHANGE of managerial personnel, or the provision of ESSENTIAL technical information — broadly MIRRORING IAS 28's own significant influence indicators internationally.</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s4">
  <span class="num">4</span>
  <h2>Mechanics — Adjusting the Investment for the Investor's Share of Profit/Loss</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cs span2">
    <div class="ctitle cs">A single-line adjustment, not full line-by-line consolidation</div>
    <div class="text-supporting">The investment is initially recorded at COST, and SUBSEQUENTLY adjusted EACH period to reflect the investor's PROPORTIONATE SHARE of the investee's profit or loss (INCREASING or DECREASING the investment's carrying amount, with a CORRESPONDING amount recognised in the investor's OWN Statement of Income as "equity in earnings of affiliates," 持分法による投資損益) — as well as its share of OTHER equity changes (e.g. the investee's OWN Valuation and Translation Adjustments movements).</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s5">
  <span class="num">5</span>
  <h2>Elimination of Unrealised Profits on Transactions With Affiliates</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cd span2">
    <div class="ctitle cd">Eliminated to the extent of the investor's ownership interest</div>
    <div class="text-supporting">Where the investor TRANSACTS with its equity-method affiliate (e.g. selling inventory that REMAINS unsold with the affiliate at the reporting date), any UNREALISED profit arising from that transaction is ELIMINATED, but only to the EXTENT of the investor's OWNERSHIP percentage in the affiliate — reflecting that the investor has NOT genuinely realised profit on the PORTION of the transaction effectively conducted with ITSELF, through its proportionate interest.</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s6">
  <span class="num">6</span>
  <h2>A DISTINCTIVE FEATURE — Equity Method Applies Only in Consolidated Statements</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cd span2">
    <div class="ctitle cd">Individual (non-consolidated) statements use cost, not equity method</div>
    <div class="text-supporting">A GENUINELY DISTINCTIVE feature of J-GAAP: the EQUITY METHOD is applied ONLY within an entity's CONSOLIDATED financial statements — in the entity's OWN INDIVIDUAL (non-consolidated, parent-only) financial statements, investments in affiliates (like investments in subsidiaries) are HELD AT COST, subject to impairment, under ASBJ Statement No. 10 (see the companion poster), NOT remeasured using the equity method. This CONTRASTS with SOME other jurisdictions applying IFRS, where IAS 27 offers entities the OPTION (though not a requirement) to apply the equity method in SEPARATE financial statements as well — under J-GAAP, this OPTION simply does NOT exist; the equity method is RESERVED exclusively for the consolidated reporting perspective.</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s7">
  <span class="num">7</span>
  <h2>Worked Example — Recognising the Investor's Share of Affiliate Profit</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cw span2">
    <div class="ctitle cw">Increasing the investment carrying amount and recognising equity in earnings</div>
    <div class="worked worked--flush">
      <div class="wk-title">Example: A 30% investment in an affiliate</div>
      <div class="wk-body">A company holds a 30% interest in an affiliate (significant influence, no control), initially recorded at ¥900,000,000. The affiliate reports net profit of ¥200,000,000 for the year.</div>
      <div class="wk-answer">The investor recognises its SHARE of the affiliate's profit: 30% × ¥200,000,000 =<strong>¥60,000,000</strong>— INCREASING the investment's carrying amount to ¥960,000,000 (¥900,000,000 + ¥60,000,000), with a MATCHING ¥60,000,000 recognised as "equity in earnings of affiliates" in the investor's CONSOLIDATED Statement of Income.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s8">
  <span class="num">8</span>
  <h2>Worked Example — Eliminating an Unrealised Intercompany Profit</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card ci span2">
    <div class="ctitle ci">Adjusting for the investor's own proportionate interest</div>
    <div class="worked worked--flush">
      <div class="wk-title">Example: Inventory sold to an affiliate, remaining unsold at year end</div>
      <div class="wk-body">A company (30% affiliate ownership) sells goods to the affiliate at a ¥50,000,000 profit margin. At year end, the affiliate has NOT yet resold these goods to outside third parties.</div>
      <div class="wk-answer">The investor ELIMINATES its PROPORTIONATE share of the unrealised profit: 30% × ¥50,000,000 =<strong>¥15,000,000</strong>— REDUCING the recognised equity-method profit accordingly, since this PORTION of the profit is considered UNREALISED from the CONSOLIDATED group's own economic perspective.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s9">
  <span class="num">9</span>
  <h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cd span2">
    <div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 16 requires</div>
    <div class="check-list"><span>List of significant affiliates accounted for under the equity method, and ownership percentages</span><span>Summarised financial information of significant equity-method affiliates</span><span>Amount of equity in earnings of affiliates recognised for the period</span></div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s10">
  <span class="num">10</span>
  <h2>Critical Judgments & Estimates</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cn span2">
    <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
        <div class="dot-list"><span>Whether significant influence genuinely exists, particularly near the 20% voting rights threshold or based on qualitative indicators alone</span></div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
        <div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of identifiable assets/liabilities at acquisition, where the investment includes an implicit goodwill-like premium</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s11">
  <span class="num">11</span>
  <h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card ci span2">
    <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IAS 28</div>
    <div class="td-table">
      <div class="th cols-12-12-12"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 16)</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS (IAS 28)</span></div>
      <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Significant influence threshold</span><span>20%–50%, plus qualitative indicators</span><span>20%–50%, plus qualitative indicators — converged</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt cols-12-12-12"><span>Unrealised profit elimination</span><span>Limited to the investor's ownership percentage</span><span>Limited to the investor's ownership percentage — converged</span></div>
      <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Equity method in separate/individual financial statements</span><span>NOT available — cost only</span><span>An OPTION available under IAS 27, though not required</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="note">The CORE equity method mechanics are genuinely CONVERGED with IAS 28 — the notable divergence lies in J-GAAP's stricter reservation of the equity method to CONSOLIDATED reporting only.</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s12">
  <span class="num">12</span>
  <h2>Statement Mapping</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cs span2">
    <div class="ctitle cs">Where every equity method event lands</div>
    <div class="td-table">
      <div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
      <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Share of affiliate profit/loss</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Consolidated statements only</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s13">
  <span class="num">13</span>
  <h2>Related Standards</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cd span2">
    <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
    <div class="td-table">
      <div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
      <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 10</span><span>Supplies the cost-based measurement applied to affiliate investments in the entity's own individual financial statements</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 22</span><span>Consolidated Financial Statements — the broader consolidation framework this Statement operates within</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s14">
  <span class="num">14</span>
  <h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cn span2">
    <div class="glossary-item">
      <div class="glossary-term">Equity method (持分法)</div>
      <div class="glossary-def">A measurement approach adjusting an investment's carrying amount for the investor's proportionate share of the investee's profit/loss and other equity changes.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last">
      <div class="glossary-term">Significant influence</div>
      <div class="glossary-def">The power to participate in an investee's financial and operating policy decisions without full control, generally presumed at 20%–50% voting rights.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="legend">
  <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
  <div class="lrow"><span class="badge bs">BS</span>Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)<span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span>Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)<span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span>純資産の部<span class="badge be">SCNA</span>Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)<span class="badge bc">SCF</span>Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</div>
</div>
  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
